          "caption": "A male Narina Trogon in breeding condition, perched in Pigeonwood in Oribi Gorge, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. The nominate race has greener (i.e. less coppery) plumage than those northwards, with turquoise face lappets in the breeding season. This individual has partially green lappets, possibly a consequence of displaying. The bare green throat patch is also visible. Females have brown face and chest plumage, and smaller lappets.",
